        "innocentReading": "A loss-leader bid for prestige: a near-zero fee buys a place on India's largest strategic sale. BS carries this explanation twice. An unnamed source says 'For Deloitte, this may be a prestigious deal and will add to its portfolio a national energy company'. Partha Bhattacharya, Coal India chairman at the time of its IPO, says bankers 'don't look at the cash money... could have gone for a notional token figure to get their name associated with this'. Under L1 (lowest-bidder) selection, a Re 1 bid wins on price.",
