        "denialFound": "No denial found from the party concerned, and none is needed: the Union Government itself made this change. From memory rather than an opened source, the CBDT/PIB press release of 10 May 2016 framed the protocol as tackling \"treaty abuse and round tripping of funds attributed to the India-Mauritius treaty\". That is an admission by the governing party, not a denial, and it should be opened and cited. Mauritius (its government and FSC) has repeatedly rejected being described as a round-tripping haven. The KSL abstract notes the \"win-win\" ties and that Mauritius is only \"considered a tax haven\". No specific rejoinder was pulled for this claim, and Mauritius was not asked.",
