        "denialFound": "Yes. The Buchs issued a joint statement on 11 Aug 2024, carried by NewsOnAir (same URL as the cited source): \"the allegations are untrue and that their life and finances are an open book ... all disclosures as required have already been furnished to SEBI over the years\"; \"The alleged investments reportedly date back to 2015, well before Madhabi Buch's appointment as a full-time member of SEBI in 2017\". This is already recorded as contra c027. There were further, widely reported points: the fund CIO Anil Ahuja was Dhaval Buch's childhood friend, the fund never invested in Adani securities, and 360 ONE WAM said the Buchs' investment was under 1.5% of fund inflows and the fund held no Adani shares. I remember these but did not re-fetch them in this pass (search budget exhausted), so they should be sourced before being added. Separately, the Lokpal dismissed the related complaints on 28 May 2025 (c028).",
