        "innocentReading": "The Aug 2023 framework was built quickly and had two separate tests. The concentration test addresses MPS/SAST evasion by promoters, the Adani concern. The size test addresses LBC/Press Note 3 screening. Once it was running, very large, widely held funds (for example university endowments, and funds concentrated in companies with no promoter) were caught even though they carry none of the promoter round-tripping risk. SEBI consulted in public three times (Feb 2024, Jul 2024, Jan 2025) and exempted only those classes, each with conditions (India AUM under 25% of global AUM; a 3% cap on the apex company). It also indexed the size threshold to market growth. The concentration test that caught Adani-linked FPIs was left as it was. The same board meeting set up a conflict-of-interest committee for SEBI's own leadership.",
