        "denialFound": "No specific denial found. The allegation has not been put to the Government of India, so none was sought. The official stated purpose runs directly against the claim. The Government of India press release of 10 May 2016, as summarised by TaxGuru (https://taxguru.in/income-tax/indiamauritius-dtaa-amended-tackle-tripping-funds.html) and STEP (https://www.step.org/industry-news/mauritius-and-india-agree-taxation-round-tripped-investments), says the protocol aims at \"tackling the dual problem of treaty shopping and round tripping of funds.\" That is a statement of purpose, not a denial.",
        "innocentReading": "Grandfathering is standard legal-certainty practice. It avoids retroactively taxing gains that thousands of legitimate PE, VC and FPI funds priced under the old treaty, which matters especially after the Vodafone retrospective-tax backlash. The protocol also treated every investor using the route the same way. The grandfathering covers only capital-gains taxing rights on shares. It never protected round-tripped money from source-of-funds liability: the Black Money Act, Income Tax Act s.68/69 on unexplained credits, PMLA and FEMA all still apply. So even as a mechanism, \"escape\" overstates what the clause did. The honest version is about effect, not design: pre-2017 Mauritius-routed positions, including any round-tripped ones, keep the old capital-gains treatment. GAAR Rule 10U(1)(d) also exempts gains on investments made before 1 April 2017, which widens that effect and should be recorded.",
        "reason": "The only source (K&L Gates, 18 May 2016) backs the mechanism and nothing more: \"Gain from the sale or transfer of shares acquired before April 1, 2017, regardless of when sold or transferred, is 'grandfathered' under the old rules.\" It says nothing about design intent, round-tripping beneficiaries, or anyone lobbying for the clause. \"Designed to let round-tripped money escape\" joins a true mechanism to an assumed motive. The record's own strongestCounter and whatWouldChangeThis admit there is no evidence of intent. The official stated purpose was the opposite: to tackle round-tripping. Grandfathering is the norm, so it cannot discriminate. \"Speculative\" is not a contract tier, and the claim as worded has no tier it can hold. Keep only a restated, effect-only analytic narrative.",
