        "denialFound": "None found for the \"control household savings\" narrative itself. Nobody put this narrative to BlackRock or JFS, and it is a circulating claim, not an allegation made by a named party. The on-record BlackRock statement is from the 2018 DSP exit (spokesperson Anthony Arthur: \"India remains a strategic market for BlackRock globally\"), quoted in https://www.business-standard.com/article/reuters/blackrock-exits-mutual-fund-venture-with-dsp-group-118050701042_1.html. The JV's own release credits the NFO to \"over 90 institutional investors\" and \"over 67,000 retail investors\".",
        "innocentReading": "A new 50:50 JV AMC starts the usual way, with cash and debt NFOs that corporate treasuries fill for cash management. Under the SEBI (Mutual Funds) Regulations 1996, scheme assets belong to unit-holders. The trustee holds them through a custodian, and the AMC only manages them for a fee. BlackRock's economic interest is half of the AMC's fee income, not the assets. At ~0.2-0.25% of industry AUM, among 47 AMCs and behind much larger foreign-sponsored AMCs, this is ordinary market entry.",
